  <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
  <h2 class="hd">It asks about the person, not the product.</h2>
  <ol class="steps">
    <li><h3>It interviews the family about who they were</h3><p>Their stories, habits, hobbies, talents, and the ten words that describe them &mdash; drawn out the way a good biographer would, not collected on a form.</p></li>
    <li><h3>It narrows thousands of options to a few that fit</h3><p>Instead of handing a grieving family a catalogue, it proposes what suits the person it just heard about, and helps them choose between the finalists.</p></li>
    <li><h3>They see the memorial, priced, as it is built</h3><p>Form, stone, lettering, emblem and inscription, with the price moving as the design does. Families who can see their options usually choose more than they would have.</p></li>
    <li><h3>You get the order written out in full</h3><p>An approved proof with a complete specification, ready for whichever monument company you use &mdash; so what comes back is what the family approved.</p></li>
  </ol>
